module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.AssociatedSite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.SchemeStack
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.SmoothAlgebraicStack
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ChangeOfSites.ChosenEtaleSite

/-!
# The lisse-étale site of an algebraic stack

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack over `S`. Stacks 0787 calls an object `x` of `𝒳`, lying over a
scheme `U` over `S`, *smooth* when the 1-morphism `x : U → 𝒳` it names under the 2-Yoneda lemma
is a smooth 1-morphism of algebraic stacks, and takes the full subcategory of the smooth objects.
A family of morphisms of smooth objects covers when the family of schemes underneath it is one of
the chosen *étale* covering families of the big site, and the topology is the one those families
generate.

Reading `x : U → 𝒳` as a 1-morphism of algebraic stacks is what distinguishes this site from its
sibling the flat-fppf site of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf`: its source has to be an object
of the 2-category of algebraic stacks, and that is **Stacks 03YS**, part (3) — the big fppf site
of a scheme over `S` is a Deligne-Mumford, hence algebraic, stack — through the object
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.schemeStack` it supplies.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.smoothObject`: smoothness of an object of an algebraic stack over `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale`: the full subcategory of the smooth objects.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.inclusion` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.toSchemes`: its inclusion into the objects of the stack,
  and the functor to the schemes of the big site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.IsCovering`: the covering families.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.precoverage` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.topology`: the precoverage and the Grothendieck
  topology it generates.

## Implementation notes

`smoothObject` applies `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.AlgebraicStacks.IsSmooth` (**Stacks 075U**) to the
1-morphism `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.objectMorphism` of the 2-Yoneda lemma, read as a 1-morphism of
algebraic stacks out of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.schemeStack`. Unfolding both abbreviations, it is
the existential smooth-diagram criterion of **Stacks 06FM**, condition (2), for smoothness of
morphisms of algebraic spaces; it is the analogue of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.flatObject`, with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSmooth` in place of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFlat`.

The covering predicate keeps the *family-level* condition of the ambient site rather than only
asking that the generated sieve cover, exactly as the flat-fppf site does; but where that site
inherits the fppf families of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.IsCovering`, this one inherits the
étale families `AlgebraicGeometry.etaleCovering` (**Stacks 03FF**) of the big site itself, so the
family is pushed all the way down to `B.Schemes` along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.toSchemes`. Every arrow of a category fibred in groupoids is
cartesian, so no cartesianness clause is needed. The topology is the Grothendieck topology
generated by exactly those families.

Essential smallness of this site — what makes sheafification, and hence its topos, available —
is `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.essentiallySmall_fullSubsite`, which is stated for an arbitrary full
subcategory of the objects of a category fibred in groupoids and so covers this site and the
flat-fppf one at once.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03FF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03YS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03YS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 075U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/075U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0787](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0787)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

universe u w

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
variable (𝒳 : Stack.AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS)

/-- The smooth objects of an algebraic stack `𝒳` over `S`: an object `x` is *smooth* when the
1-morphism it names under the 2-Yoneda lemma, from the big fppf site of the scheme it lies over —
an algebraic stack by **Stacks 03YS**, part (3) — is a smooth 1-morphism of algebraic stacks in
the sense of **Stacks 075U**. -/
abbrev smoothObject : ObjectProperty 𝒳.val.val.obj :=
  fun x ↦ AlgebraicStacks.IsSmooth B S hS
    (Bicategory.InducedBicategory.mkHom
        (objectMorphism B S hS 𝒳.val (Functor.Fiber.mk (a := x) rfl)) :
      schemeStack.{u, w} B S hS (𝒳.val.val.p.obj x) ⟶ 𝒳)

/-- The full subcategory of the smooth objects of an algebraic stack over `S`. -/
@[stacks 0787 "the lisse-etale site: its underlying category of smooth objects"]
abbrev LisseEtale := (smoothObject.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳).FullSubcategory

namespace LisseEtale

/-- The inclusion of the smooth objects of an algebraic stack into all of its objects. -/
abbrev inclusion : LisseEtale.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳 ⥤ 𝒳.val.val.obj :=
  (smoothObject.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳).ι

/-- The scheme of the big site underneath a smooth object of an algebraic stack over `S`. -/
abbrev toSchemes : LisseEtale.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳 ⥤ B.Schemes :=
  inclusion.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳 ⋙ 𝒳.val.val.p ⋙ BigFppfOver.forget B S hS

/-- A family of morphisms of smooth objects of an algebraic stack covers when the family of
schemes underneath it is a chosen étale covering family of the big site. -/
@[stacks 0787 "the lisse-etale site: its coverings"]
abbrev IsCovering (E : Covering (LisseEtale.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳)) : Prop :=
  etaleCovering B
    ⟨(toSchemes.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳).obj E.1, E.2.map (toSchemes.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳)⟩

/-- The precoverage of the lisse-étale site: the families of smooth objects inherited from the
chosen étale covering families of the big site. -/
def precoverage : Precoverage (LisseEtale.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳) where
  coverings U := {R | ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} U,
    R = E.presieve₀ ∧ IsCovering.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳 ⟨U, E⟩}

/-- The Grothendieck topology of the lisse-étale site: the one generated by the inherited étale
covering families between smooth objects. -/
@[stacks 0787 "the lisse-etale site: its Grothendieck topology"]
abbrev topology : GrothendieckTopology (LisseEtale.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳) :=
  (precoverage.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳).toGrothendieck

end LisseEtale

end AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

end
